Hello,

This is an e-mail to remind everyone about the Buildroot Developers
Meeting that will take place right after FOSDEM in Brussels, on
February 1-2. We have a Wiki page about this event:

  http://elinux.org/Buildroot:DeveloperDaysFOSDEM2016

Eleven participants have already registered. If you are a Buildroot
developer and want to attend, please let us know, it is not too late to
register (participation is free).

Also, whether you will participate physically to the event or not, you
are very much encouraged to suggest some topics that should be
discussed. If you cannot attend, we can arrange some remote discussion
(via IRC or Google Hangout) during the meeting. A significant number of
core Buildroot developers will be at the meeting, so it is the perfect
time to take some decisions on specific technical topics.

Thanks for your participation,

Thomas
